INSERT INTO `eventdb` VALUES ('Trend setters',1,'19.09.2026','11:30AM-12:45PM','KAMARAJAJAR OPEN AUDITORIUM',2,1,1,2,2,'COMMON','public/images/event/29329_1788929658.jpg','On Stage','A 3-stage duo fashion competition featuring a runway showcase, a concept & dress presentation, and a live Q&A defense with eliminations at each stage.  Rules: Team size: 2 participants (1 Designer + 1 Model, or 2 Models). Round 1 (Runway Walk): 2–3 minutes per pair to showcase outfits on stage; bottom teams eliminated. Round 2 (Concept & Styling Pitch): Qualifying pairs get 2 minutes to explain the theme, material choice, and outfit design philosophy. Round 3 (Judge Q&A Defense): Finalists undergo a 2-minute live cross-interrogation by the jury on design and styling. Audio track must be submitted 1 hour in advance. Decent attire mandatory; fire, liquids, and hazardous props strictly banned.  Judging Criteria: Outfit styling & ramp poise (35%), concept clarity & design depth (30%), Q&A response & spontaneity (20%), overall stage impact (15%). ','-'),('Sync or Sink (Western Dance Battle)',2,'18.09.2026','1:30PM-5.00PM','KAMARAJAJAR OPEN AUDITORIUM',12,1,1,12,12,'COMMON','public/images/event/29330.jpg','On Stage','group formations, and rhythm execution across modern western dance styles.  Rules: Team size: 6–12  participants. Time limit: 4–6 minutes (including stage setup and clearance). Styles permitted include Hip-Hop, Popping, Locking, Breaking, Contemporary, House, or Krump (fusion with classical or folk styles is strictly restricted). Audio track must be submitted in MP3 format via USB drive to the sound console at least 1 hour before the competition. Obscene gestures, offensive track lyrics, or dangerous stage props (fire, powder, liquids, glass) will lead to direct disqualification. At foot loose (2 Minutes) the Main / lead dancers will be given rest to evaluate the team Sync coordination.   Judging Criteria: Choreography & movement complexity (35%), synchronization & team coordination (30%), musicality & rhythm accuracy (20%), stage presence, energy & costumes (15%). ','-'),('. Gramathu Ragam (Folk Group Showdown)',3,'19.09.2026','9:45AM-11:00AM','KAMARAJAJAR OPEN AUDITORIUM',12,1,1,12,12,'COMMON','public/images/event/29331.jpg','On Stage','A high-energy group folk dance competition celebrating indigenous culture, traditional art forms, dynamic expressions, and coordinated regional rhythms.  Rules: Team size: 6–12 participants. Time limit: 4–6 minutes (including stage setup and clearance). Dance forms must strictly feature authentic Indian folk styles (e.g., Karagattam, Oyilattam, Kavadiyattam, Kolattam, Thappattam/Parai, Bhangra, Garba, Lavani); fusion with cinematic or western styles is prohibited. Audio tracks must be submitted in MP3 format 1 hour prior to the event, or live traditional acoustic percussion can be used on stage. Traditional attire representing the chosen folk style is mandatory. Dangerous props (fire, oil lamps, live glass, sharp weapons) and messy substances (powders, colors, liquids) are strictly prohibited. At foot loose(2 Minutes) the dancers are asked to completely change their positions & use the property mention by the jury at that time to evaluate the team coordination.  Judging Criteria: Cultural authenticity & folk style representation (35%), synchronization, formations & rhythm (30%), facial expressions & energy (20%), costume appropriateness & traditional prop handling (15%). ','-'),(' Orchestra: Group Singing & Music ',4,'16.09.2026','3','KAMARAJAJAR OPEN AUDITORIUM',12,1,1,12,12,'COMMON','public/images/event/29332.jpg','On Stage','A competitive live musical showcase featuring vocal harmonies and synchronized acoustic or electric live instrumental orchestration.  Rules: Team size: 6–12 participants (including vocalists and instrumentalists). Time limit: 8–10 minutes (strictly includes 3 minutes for stage setup/sound check and 5–7 minutes of live performance). Pre-recorded backing tracks, programmed MIDI sequences, rhythm loops, and vocal processors/auto-tune are strictly prohibited; 100% of all sounds must be produced live on stage. Standard 5-piece drum kit, basic backline amplifiers, and vocal microphones are provided by the organizers; teams must bring their own personal instruments, cables, processors, and special percussions. Obscene lyrics, defamatory statements, or offensive gestures lead to immediate disqualification.  Judging Criteria: Vocal harmony, pitch accuracy & dynamic range (35%), instrumental synchronization & arrangement complexity (30%), rhythm stability, tempo control & stage presence (20%), overall sound balance & song medley transition (15%). ','-'),(' Shadow Theatre (Bommalattam) ',5,'15.09.2026','3:00PM-5:00PM','KAMARAJAJAR OPEN AUDITORIUM',8,1,1,8,8,'COMMON','public/images/event/29333.jpg','On Stage','erformers use a backlit white screen to tell a complete narrative solely using bodily silhouettes, hands, and minimal props.   Rules: Team size: 5–8 participants. Duration: 5 minutes max (including setup and performance). The act must convey a clear social or cultural message. Performances must rely on bodily silhouettes, shadow play, and traditional puppetry/Bommalattam props behind the screen. Backlit screen and lighting will be provided by organizers; teams must bring their own cutout props and materials. Background music/voice track (MP3) must be submitted 1 hour prior to the event. Any offensive content or vulgarity leads to immediate disqualification.   Judging Criteria: Silhouette clarity & puppetry execution (35%), storytelling flow & thematic message (35%), shadow prop innovation & creativity (30%).  ','-'),('Flash Mob Fusion',6,'16.09.2026','9:45AM-11:00AM','',40,1,1,40,40,'COMMON','public/images/event/29334.jpg','Off Stage','1.Teams perform an unannounced multi-genre dance routine across designated high-footfall / sports ground on campus.  \r\n2.Team size: 30–40. Duration: 4–6 minutes. Track must blend at least 3 distinct musical styles (e.g., Folk, Hip-Hop, Classical, Retro). Must include a mandatory 2minute extra dance \"Tricky 4-Way Direction Shift\" segment where the entire crew rapidly changes facing directions (North, South, East, West) in perfect synchronization without breaking rhythm. Dancers must blend into the campus crowd beforehand and disperse completely within 30 seconds after the performance. Pathways must remain unblocked; fire, party poppers, powders, and liquids are banned. Audio track (MP3) must be submitted 2 hours in advance. ','-'),('Short Film Screening',7,'15.09.2026','1:30PM-2:45PM','',12,1,1,12,12,'COMMON','public/images/event/29336.jpg','Off Stage','1.Team size: 10-12. All actors, directors, cinematographers, editors, and musicians must strictly be students from the same registered team. Teams must submit a mandatory 1-minute unedited BTS (Behind-The-Scenes) verification video showing the registered student cast and crew working on set and in post-production. Total runtime must not exceed 10 minutes (including credits).\r\n2. Submissions must be in 1080p MP4/MOV format on a USB drive and tested at the console 2 hours prior to avoid technical glitches. English subtitles are mandatory. Any outside professional assistance or plagiarism results in immediate disqualification. Note: no caste, no political content. ','-'),('Kshatriya Clash',8,'11.09.2026','11:30AM-12:45PM','',6,1,1,6,6,'COMMON','public/images/event/29337.jpg','Off Stage','1.Open to individual performers or teams of up to 6 participants. \r\n2.Time limit: 4–6 minutes (including setup and clearing of performance gear). Permitted disciplines include traditional martial arts (Silambam, Kalaripayattu, Karate, Taekwondo), acrobatic martial arts, stage combat choreography, and safe physical strength feats (breaking tiles,flexibility demonstrations). \r\n3.Live-edge metal blades, unblunted sharp weapons, fire stunts, and unsafe glass props are strictly prohibited; only competition-grade blunt weapons, bamboo/rattan sticks (Silambam kambu), or safe practice gear are allowed. Safety mats will be provided on stage. Audio tracks (MP3) must be submitted 1 hour prior. Reckless maneuvers endangering the audience, judges, or fellow participants result in immediate disqualification.','-'),('Media AND  RJ Studio ',9,'','3:00PM-5:00PM','',5,1,1,5,5,'COMMON','public/images/event/29338.jpg','Off Stage','1.Team size: 5 participants. (includes two on-stage presenter & three phone callers) Preparation time: 10 minutes. Performance time: 3–5 minutes + 1 minute mockcaller interaction. Languages permitted: English, Tamil, or conversational bilingual flow. Vulgarity, unparliamentarily language, or personal defamation leads to immediate disqualification.  2.Judging Criteria: Voice modulation & clarity (35%), spontaneity & presence of mind (35%), content engagement & pacing (30%).','-'),('Human Chess ',10,'15.09.2026','9:45AM-11:00AM','',20,1,1,20,20,'COMMON','public/images/event/29339.jpg','Off Stage','1.Team size: 20 participants. (including 4 instructors). The match is played on a giant 10 m x 10m  ground board where live costumed participants represent the chess pieces. Four student strategists command the game from elevated  platforms. \r\n2.Time limit: 10 minute. When a piece is captured, the involved actors must execute a 10 to 15-second choreographed duel/battle routine before the captured piece leaves the board. Physical contact during duels must strictly follow non-injurious staged choreography; weapon props must be made of safe foam or wood (metal items strictly banned). Standard blitz chess rules apply for illegal moves and time outs.  \r\n3. Judging Criteria: Strategic chess gameplay & tactical victory (40%), combat choreography & duel synchronization (35%), costume authenticity, theme aesthetics & stage presence (25%).  ','-'),('Mixology Challenge',11,'11.09.2026','01:30 PM – 02:45 PM','',2,0,0,0,2,'BOYS','public/images/event/Gemini_Generated_Image_mw4l91mw4l91mw4l.png','Off Stage','1. Solo event or duo. Time limit: 5 minutes. \r\n2. No glass bottles for juggling (plastic flair bottles required). \r\n3. Alcohol or hazardous liquids are banned. \r\n4. Special twist at event –participants should be ready to do with the conditions given.\r\n\r\nJudging Criteria: \r\n1.Drink flavor profile & layering (40%), flair showmanship (30%),\r\ncleanliness (30%).','-'),('Beatbox & Live Sound Effects',12,'15.09.2026','11:30 AM – 12:45 PM','',5,0,0,0,5,'BOYS','public/images/event/images.jpg','Off Stage','1. Open to solo performers to maximum 5 participants\r\n2. Time limit: 3–4 minutes per performance - 2 min for beatbox and 2 min for sound effects recreation in movie. \r\n3. All sounds, beats, basslines, and sound effects must be produced 100% organically using the mouth, throat, and vocal cords; pre-recorded audio tracks, external instruments, loop stations, and vocal effects pedals/auto-tune are strictly prohibited .\r\n4. Standard wired dynamic stage microphones will be provided.\r\n5. The performance must include a minimum of two distinct rhythmic styles or tempo shifts (e.g., Hip-Hop beat drop, EDM build-up, cinematic soundscapes, and regional folk percussion emulation). \r\n6. Obscene sounds, derogatory vocalizations, or abusive language result in immediate disqualification\r\n\r\nJudging Criteria: \r\n1. Sound clarity, technical complexity & bass punch (35%), rhythm consistency, tempo control & timing (30%), sound effect versatility & dynamic range\r\n(20%), crowd engagement, originality & stage presence (15%).','-'),('Glow in the Dark',13,'16.09.2026','11:30 AM – 12:45 PM','Kamarajar Open Auditorium',6,1,1,6,6,'BOYS','public/images/event/B03.png','On Stage','1. Team size: 2-6 participants Time limit: 4–6 minutes (including black-out stage setup and clearance).\r\n2. The performance must be executed under full stage blackout using specialized visual aids such as UV/blacklight-reactive costumes, neon body paints, glow props, LED gear, or fiber optics.\r\n3. Music tracks (MP3) must be submitted 1 hour prior to the event.\r\n4. Live fire, pyrotechnics, oil lamps, loose liquids, and toxic chemical powders are strictly prohibited\r\n5. The routine must maintain clear visual synchronization, geometric formations, and spatial awareness throughout the blackout state\r\n\r\nJudging Criteria:\r\n1. Visual impact, luminescence balance & light choreography (35%), synchronization, formations & timing precision (30%), musicality & creative concept flow (20%), costume design, prop integration & safety compliance (15%).','-'),('Street Art & Board Sketching',14,'16.09.2026','01:30 PM – 02:45 PM','',5,1,1,5,5,'BOYS','public/images/event/Gemini_Generated_Image_4zts474zts474zts.png','Off Stage','1. Open to individual to maximum 5 per team Total time duration: 1 hours.\r\n2. A standard display board / designated floor street canvas area will be allocated on-site by organizers along with the central theme announced at the start of the event.\r\n3. Permitted media include acrylics, pastels, charcoal, spray paint (non-toxic), chalk, and markers.\r\n4. Pre-drawn stencils, printed outlines, digital tracing projectors, and smartphones are strictly prohibited during the creation window.\r\n5. The artwork must be 100% original, and vulgar, political, or offensive imagery leads to immediate disqualification.\r\n\r\nJudging Criteria: \r\n1. Thematic interpretation & storytelling (35%), sketching technique,\r\nlinework & shading depth (30%), color contrast, composition & visual balance (20%),\r\nneatness, creativity & time management (15%).\r\n','-'),('RC Relay Grand Prix',15,'11.09.2026','09:45 AM – 11:00 AM','',5,1,1,5,5,'BOYS','public/images/event/Gemini_Generated_Image_s6xcxqs6xcxqs6xc.png','Off Stage','1.  Team size: Exactly 3 drivers + 2 crew for track assist 5 per team Time : 15 min (12 minutes for one race ).\r\n2. Position of Race : The driver with the fastest lap gets \"PolePosition\" (1st on the grid).\r\n3. The second fastest starts 2nd, and so on with 3 min trail The race consists of a continuous 3-lap relay where each registered driver must navigate exactly 1 full lap before passing the physical transmitter (remote controller) to the next driver in the designated pit lane box.\r\n4. Handing off the controller outside the pit box incurs a +10 second penalty.\r\n5. The track includes ramps, narrow chicanes, slalom cones, and a mandatory stop-and-go zone.\r\n6. Dislodging a boundary cone adds a +5 second penalty to the team\'s total time; flipping the car requires a marshal reset at the nearest checkpoint with a +10 second penalty.\r\n7. The team with the lowest cumulative time (including penalties) wins.\r\n\r\nJudging Criteria:\r\n1. Overall 3-lap completion time with penalty adjustments (40%), driving precision, obstacle navigation & throttle control (30%), pit-lane handoff efficiency & transition speed (20%), track discipline & rule compliance (10%).','-'),(' Fashion Art & Eco Garment Design',16,'11.09.2026','01:30 PM - 02:45 PM','',8,1,1,8,8,'GIRLS','public/images/event/gar.webp','Off Stage','1.Team size: 4–8 participants (including models and student designers). Total \r\ntime limit: 5–7 minutes (including ramp walk, outfit presentation, and a 1-minute \r\nconcept briefing by the designer).\r\n\r\n2. Costumes must be crafted using at least 80% non-hazardous recyclable, upcycled, or biodegradable materials (e.g., discarded fabric scraps, paper, cardboard, plastic bottles, jute, dried natural fibers, aluminum cans, packaging waste); standard readymade clothing is strictly prohibited.\r\n\r\n3.Outfits must be durable enough to sustain normal movement, posing, and full ramp walks without disintegrating. \r\n\r\n4.Banned items include live flame, toxic paints, sharp uncovered metal/glass edges, and \r\nhazardous chemical adhesives. \r\n\r\n5. Background track (MP3) must be submitted on a USB drive 1 hour prior to the event.\r\n\r\nJudging Criteria:\r\n\r\nEco-material innovation, upcycling technique & construction quality (35%), thematic styling,outfit aesthetics & design cohesion (30%), ramp presence, model \r\npoise & walk confidence (20%), designer concept presentation & material sustainability\r\ndefense (15%).','-'),(' Culinary Challenge with Herb Identification',17,'15.09.2026','11.30 AM - 12:45 PM','',2,1,2,2,2,'GIRLS','public/images/event/culinary challange.png','Off Stage','1.Team size: 2 , Time limit: 45 minutes , Ingredients brought by participants; basic \r\npreparation (washing/peeling) allowed beforehand, but cutting/assembling must happen \r\non spot.\r\n\r\n2.Participants must give the exact common name, regional Tamil name, or \r\nbotanical nomenclature along with one key medicinal/culinary use on the provided time.\r\n\r\n3.Special twist at event – participants should be ready to cook with the conditions given\r\n\r\nJudging Criteria:\r\n\r\nTaste balance (40%), visual presentation/plating (35%), hygiene & station cleanliness (25%)','-'),(' Reels & Meme Contest',18,'16.09.2026','01:30 PM - 02:45 PM','',5,1,5,5,5,'GIRLS','public/images/event/Reels & Meme Contest.png','Off Stage','1.Entire reel must be captured within college boundaries \r\nduring the event window.\r\n2.Stock footage is banned, Note: no caste, no political content.\r\n\r\nJudging Criteria:\r\n\r\nFraming & color grading (35%), narrative pacing (35%), adherence to \r\ntheme (30%).','-'),('Pop Culture Quiz',19,'11.09.2026','09:45 AM - 11.00 AM','',3,1,3,3,3,'GIRLS','public/images/event/Pop Culture Quiz.png','Off Stage','1.Team size 2–3 \r\n2.3 Rounds: Time : 15 Min \r\n3.Written prelims, Audio-Visual buzzer round, and Rapid Fire.\r\n\r\n\r\nJudging Criteria:\r\n \r\nCumulative points across rounds.\r\n','-'),('Recreation Round (Iconic Cinema, Song & Comedy Re-enactment)',20,'17.09.2026','03.00 PM - 05.00 PM ','',6,1,6,6,6,'GIRLS','public/images/event/Iconic Cinema, Song & Comedy Re-enactment.png','On Stage','1.Team size: 2–6 participants (actors/models and support styling crew).\r\n2.Time limit: 4–5 minutes on stage (strictly includes 1 minute for stage prop setup and 3–4 minutes for the live performance).\r\n3.Teams must recreate a legendary scene featuring a seamless blend of character styling, iconic dialogue delivery, a musical song sequence, \r\nand a mandatory comedy routine or comedic scene integration (e.g.,iconic Tamil comedy tracks or English sitcom/parody moments).\r\n4.. Outfits, facial styling, and mannerisms must closely mimic the original characters.\r\n5. Minimal hand props and lightweight set pieces are permitted; fire, liquids, powders, glass, party poppers, and hazardous items are strictly prohibited.\r\n6. The audio track (MP3) combining background scores, dialogues, and songs must be submitted to the sound coordinator 1 hour prior to the event.\r\n7.Vulgarity, double entendre, offensive slang, or personal/defamatory mockery will lead to immediate disqualification.\r\n\r\nJudging Criteria:\r\nVisual likeness, costume accuracy, makeup & aesthetic styling (35%), \r\ncomic timing, dialogue modulation, acting precision & expressions (30%), musical choreography, lip-sync/dialogue synchronization & iconic pose execution (20%), stage presence, overall entertainment value & creative scene flow (15%).','-');
/*!40000 ALTER TABLE `eventdb` ENABLE KEYS */;
